course: dictionary
lesson: 10155
title: Thud: a dull, heavy sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thud is a dull, heavy sound, like something heavy falling or hitting something soft. Read the clues around the word. «A rabbit thumps its back foot to warn other rabbits of danger, and the thud travels through the ground into the burrow.» Rabbits warn each other of danger, and the sound travels through the ground, so thud is a sound you could feel as well as hear.
explain: Thud can be a noun (a thud) or a verb (to thud). In the verb form, the sound is made by an action: «The bag thudded onto the floor.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Thud sounds different from other words for noise. A thud is dull and low, a clang is a ringing sound made by metal, and a crash is loud and breaking. Choosing the right sound word helps your reader picture the scene exactly.
fact: A thud is a dull, heavy sound made when something heavy falls or hits something soft.
fact: To thud means to fall or hit with a thud, or to beat heavily.
fact: «Thud» is an onomatopoeia: the word sounds like the noise it describes.
fact: «My heart was thudding» shows fear or excitement.
fact: A thud is dull and low, a clang is metal, and a crash is loud and breaking.
exercise: «A rabbit thumps its back foot to warn other rabbits of danger, and the thud travels through the ground.» What does thud mean in this sentence? | A quick, light jump | A soft, gentle touch | *A dull, heavy sound | A bright, ringing sound
exercise: «The bag hit the floor with a thud.» What kind of sound is a thud? | Sharp and high | Soft and sweet | Loud and metal | *Dull and heavy
exercise: «My heart was thudding.» What does thudding mean here? | Running away | Floating quietly | *Beating heavily | Singing softly
test: Which word means a loud sound of metal being hit? | thud | *clang | sigh | whisper
test: Footsteps ___ upstairs. Which word completes the sentence as a verb? | glow | melt | whisper | *thud
exam: Which sentence uses thud as a verb? | The sound of the thud woke me. | A thud is a dull sound. | The book hit the desk with a thud. | *The books thudded onto the floor.
